From 92b36908e931f770a1e8e66dc1a1b0f585b1014d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:58:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Kanban: route default-tier cards by planned budget share
 (ratio routing)

An unpinned default card now starts on the governed pool furthest below its
v2 budget share (llm_pacing.json v2.pools[p].ratio) instead of always on
kanban.default_model. Pools come from the routing class of the default
model (the level a class:<level> default names, else the level listing the
concrete model); ratio_route_models picks each pool's route. A pool is
eligible with ratio > 0, not at reserve, a known rate, enabled, a live
credential here and no wall. The share is this host+board's default-tier
run_route starts over 6 h, counted once per dispatch tick (bounded by a
binary search on the event id) and incremented per start in the tick.
Fail open (today's route) on a missing/stale/malformed v2, no eligible pool,
ratio_routing: false, or any fault (logged with traceback).

The pick is an unpinned default to the episode, wall and pace rules; the
reason is tagged default+ratio:<pool>[+move], and model_tier/run_route carry
pool, target, share and deficit. paced_route no longer moves default routes
(the governor's claim-time pace move still does); queue notes name a ratio
pick as "next run on <pool> (budget share)".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
