+**Ratio routing.** An unpinned default-tier card (no model or provider override, not a review run, no `require_model: true` line) starts on the governed pool furthest below its planned budget share instead of always on `kanban.default_model`. The pools are the providers of the `model_routing.routes` class level of `kanban.default_model`: the level a `class:<level>` default names, else the one level that lists the concrete default model (registry order; each runs `ratio_route_models.<pool>` when that is one of its routes in the level, else its first route). A pick is always a concrete model and provider, also under a class default. A pool is eligible when its fresh `v2` entry has `ratio` above 0, is not `at_reserve` and has a known `rate_tokens_per_s`, its provider is enabled, this host holds a live credential that can serve the model, and no provider wall stands. Targets are the eligible pools' ratios renormalized to 1; the share is each pool's part of this host's default-tier starts on the board over the last six hours (`run_route` receipts). The pool with the largest target minus share wins (ties: registry order). The route reason is `default+ratio:<pool>` (a later wall, episode or pace move appends its own suffix), and the `model_tier` and `run_route` receipts carry a `ratio` block (`pool`, `model`, `target`, `share`, `deficit`, `starts`). Queue notes name the pick (`next run on anthropic (budget share): anthropic/<model>`). It keeps today's route when `ratio_routing` is `false`, the `v2` document is missing, malformed or older than 20 minutes, no pool is eligible, a concrete default model is in no class level (or in two), or the choice fails; under a class default the kept route is the `class:<level>` selector itself. Start counts are read once per dispatcher tick and each start in the tick is added, so a card's preview, governor check and launch agree and the next card sees the previous start.
 
